Technical
### Changed

- Update the Anthropic, `coverlet.collector`, and `Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI` NuGet dependencies. ([#328](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/328))

### Added

- **Breaking:** Remove `description` from schema version 2 of `changelog.json` and store complete facts, including descriptions, in the run record; read fact bases from records instead of changelog files. ([#294](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/294))
- **Breaking:** Make `preview` show facts and what `generate` would send without calling a model or writing output; use `generate --no-publish` to render without publishing. ([#292](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/292))
- Show each run’s outcome in its opening summary, identify audience renderings by name, print the command header, and group help options. ([#342](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/342))
- Group `doctor` checks by Repository, Model, and GitHub, mark their statuses, and report whether warnings would prevent a run. ([#341](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/341))
- Show run progress with the Quiet Pulse spinner in supported terminals and add `--plain` to every command. ([#340](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/340))
- Quote pull request titles and descriptions in prompts, escape embedded title and description tags, and cut descriptions longer than 8,000 characters in prompts. ([#338](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/338))
- Refuse to replace a published release unless `generate` is given `--replace-published`, checking before model calls and again when writing. ([#335](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/335))
- Have `doctor` identify the version-specific configuration template when `chartula.yaml` is missing. ([#329](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/329))
- Display run progress for pull request reading, audience rendering, and checks, with plain output when no terminal is available. ([#297](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/297))
- Add `chartula doctor` to check the setup a run needs, including repository, model, and GitHub access. ([#295](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/295))
- Use the text read by the model at each `factBase.depth` to determine closed issue numbers, and treat `title-description-and-issues`, `full`, and `issues` as `title-and-description`. ([#293](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/293))
- Include direct commits without pull requests as changes, skip merge commits without pull requests, and record the counts of both in the run record. ([#291](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/291))
- Add `chartula --version` to print the installed informational version before reading configuration or repository data. ([#286](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/286))
- Allow a first tag to start at the first commit and require confirmation before reading a first or large range; use `--yes` to confirm without interaction. ([#282](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/282))

### Fixed

- List each CLI option once under its correct help group and update the documentation and roadmap. ([#344](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/344))
- Compare rendering names and facts with whitespace folded and code fences removed, without matching across separate facts. ([#336](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/336))
- Write a fixed sentence to technical changelog and release-note outputs when no technical rendering exists, while keeping `renderings.technical` empty. ([#333](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/333))
- Use relaxed JSON escaping for `changelog.json` and the run record so their contents remain readable while escaping only what JSON requires. ([#332](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/332))
- Separate review flags from rendering text with a blank line and a `Flagged for review:` heading. ([#331](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/331))
- Report a credential variable as unset in the run header when it is blank or unset, while continuing to name the variable without exposing its value. ([#330](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/330))
- Validate command-line options before a command starts, reject unknown or unsupported options and missing values, and honor `-h` and `--help` after a command. ([#301](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/301))
- Append a trailing slash to `Chartula__GitHub__ApiBaseUrl` when it is missing so relative API requests resolve correctly. ([#290](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/290))
- Read an empty `filter.excludeCategories` list as an explicit empty value that drops no categories. ([#289](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/289))
- Distinguish model answers the SDK cannot read from requests that could not reach the endpoint, and include the unreadable answer’s value in the error message. ([#288](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/288))
- Refuse to load configuration when both `chartula.yaml` and `chartula.yml` are present, and report both paths. ([#287](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/287))
- Check whether a token can publish before the first model call in `generate`; skip the check for `preview` and `generate --no-publish`. ([#285](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/285))
- Clarify that `--no-publish` writes every file and omits only GitHub release notes. ([#284](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/284))

